        {
          "say": "It looks like the point moves one place right.",
          "write": "× 10 → 1 place right"
        },
        {
          "say": "Times 1000 moves it 3 places. Add a zero placeholder.",
          "write": "3.42 × 1000 = 3420"
        },
        {
          "say": "Divide by 100. The point moves 2 places left.",
          "write": "58.6 ÷ 100 = 0.586"
        },
        {
          "say": "Count the zeros to know how many places.",
          "write": "zeros = jumps"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Multiplying decimals",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Work out 0.4 times 0.3. First ignore the points.",
          "write": "4 × 3 = 12"
        },
        {
          "say": "Count the decimal places. One plus one is two.",
          "write": "1 + 1 = 2 places"
        },
        {
          "say": "Put two places back in the answer.",
          "write": "0.4 × 0.3 = 0.12"
        },
        {
          "say": "Tenths times tenths make hundredths. Twelve small squares out of 100.",
          "diagram": "diagrams/y7/maths/multiplying-and-dividing-decimals-area.svg",
          "alt": "0.4 by 0.3 rectangle in a hundred square"
        },
        {
          "say": "2.6 times 1.4. Twenty-six times 14 is 364. Two places back.",
          "write": "2.6 × 1.4 = 3.64"
        },
        {
          "say": "Estimate: 3 times 1 is 3. 3.64 is close.",
          "write": "≈ 3 ✓"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Dividing by a whole number",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Share 9 dollars 36 between 4 people.",
          "write": "9.36 ÷ 4"
        },
        {
          "say": "The point in the answer sits right above the point inside.",
          "write": "point on the roof"
        },
        {
          "say": "9 divided by 4 is 2, remainder 1. Carry it.",
          "write": "9 ÷ 4 = 2 r 1"
        },
        {
          "say": "13 divided by 4 is 3, remainder 1. Then 16 divided by 4 is 4.",
          "write": "13 ÷ 4 = 3 r 1,  16 ÷ 4 = 4"
        },
        {
          "say": "Each person pays 2 dollars 34.",
          "write": "$2.34"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Dividing by a decimal",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "7.2 divided by 0.06. Make the divisor a whole number.",
          "write": "7.2 ÷ 0.06"
        },
        {
          "say": "Multiply both numbers by 100. The answer doesn't change.",
          "write": "× 100 both"
        },
        {
          "say": "Now it is 720 divided by 6, which is 120.",
          "write": "720 ÷ 6 = 120"
        },
        {
          "say": "Like 6 divided by 3 equals 60 divided by 30.",
          "write": "6 ÷ 3 = 60 ÷ 30"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Does the answer make sense?",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Times a number less than 1 makes it smaller.",
          "write": "5 × 0.8 = 4",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 220,
            "alt": "5 shrinks to 4",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 40,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 400,
                "h": 50,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "5"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 40,
                "y": 140,
                "w": 320,
                "h": 50,
                "fill": "orange",
                "change": "add",
                "label": "5 × 0.8 = 4"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Divide by a number less than 1 makes it bigger.",
          "write": "5 ÷ 0.8 = 6.25",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 220,
            "alt": "5 grows to 6.25",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 40,
                "y": 60,
                "w": 400,
                "h": 50,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "5"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 40,
                "y": 140,
                "w": 500.0,
                "h": 50,
                "fill": "green",
                "change": "add",
                "label": "5 ÷ 0.8 = 6.25"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Estimate first. It helps you catch a point in the wrong place.",
          "write": "estimate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Watch out for these",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Don't line up the points when multiplying.",
          "write": "multiply, then count"
        },
        {
          "say": "Count places in both numbers. 0.5 times 0.3 is 0.15.",
          "write": "✗ 1.5   ✓ 0.15"
        },
        {
          "say": "Dividing by 10 makes it smaller. 45.2 divided by 10 is 4.52.",
          "write": "45.2 ÷ 10 = 4.52"
        },
        {
          "say": "Change both numbers. 6.3 divided by 0.09 becomes 630 divided by 9.",
          "write": "630 ÷ 9 = 70"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Remember",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Count, multiply, put them back.",
          "write": "count, multiply, put back"
        },
        {
          "say": "Zeros tell you the jumps.",
          "write": "× 1000 → 3 places"
        },
        {
          "say": "Same move to both numbers when dividing by a decimal.",
          "write": "same move to both"
        },
        {
          "say": "Point on the roof in short division.",
          "write": "point on the roof"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}